For this we will present a Business Promotion Act to further the following aims:
- To facilitate and encourage the creation of new businesses;
- To support the growth of young innovative companies;
- To improve financing for SMEs;
- To reduce administrative burdens;
- To encourage consolidation and growth;
- To promote internationalisation.

The EU is not a peaceful actor, but encourages the rearmament of Member States and is not oriented towards initiatives that lead to the democratisation of the United Nations, peace, disarmament or to a substantial increase in cooperation to end hunger and poverty, which are themselves weapons of mass destruction par excellence. The United Left is committed to substantially changing the current Foreign and Neighbourhood Policy of the EU. This should be based on peace, disarmament, cooperation and democratic international relations. We suggest the use of an International Convention on Disarmament to ensure:
- The prohibition and ecologically-friendly destruction of the entire arsenal of weapons of mass destruction;
- The drastic reduction of industrial and research and development programmes on armaments to zero;
- Strict application of the code of conduct on arms exports;
- The diplomatic prevention of conflicts and the renunciation of war.

Venstre wants an EU that: 
- Has effective institutions which ensure that right goes before might, so larger countries and companies cannot dominate others because of their sheer size;
- The EU’s administration must be transparent;
- Respects the principle of subsidiarity so that decisions are made as close to the citizens as possible.

